                      see this either -- the same lesson as d_returnzero.

 d_lessthan    35/35  EXPECTED NOT TO DIE, and that is the point.  Over the
                      reachable guest domain len is one of {1,2,4,8}, so
                      `len < 8' and `len != 8' select the same set.  A mutant
                      that will not die is a RESULT: it records that the guard's
                      FORM is immaterial and only its ACCEPT SET matters, which
                      is what d_accept4 attacks.  If it DOES die, my domain claim
                      is wrong and I want to know.

 e_swapsite    34/35  ONLY `xsite order'.  All six literals survive exactly once
                      (verified by dry run: declines=1 for each), so `xsite 6msg'
                      stays GREEN and only the ORDER row can see it.  This is the
                      mutant that proves `xsite order' is not vacuous; without it
                      every mutant that reds the order row also reds 6msg.

